 ### Multiple submission queues
-Multiple submission queues is a solution where GPU commands are submitted to specific queues instead of directly to the GPU. Barriers only enforce dependencies between tasks of the same queue, allowing tasks in different queues to run independently [S1, unofficial]. Submit task C to a different queue than task A and B to let it run independently of A or B [S1, unofficial]. Vulkan reports 24 queues for Nvidia GPUs, 16 for AMD, 5 for Intel, and usually only 1 for mobiles [S1, unofficial]. CUDA lets you have an unlimited number of streams, but behind the scenes maps them to 32 internal queues [S1, unofficial]. The restricted number of queues is not enough for micro-dependencies. Modern GPUs can have 50 to 100 cores, so it is not possible to use queues to enforce dependencies at the GPU core granularity [S1, unofficial].
